# docs/book/06-structs-enums.md:46 § "Methods" writes
# `return (self.x * self.x + self.y * self.y) as float` on float fields -- an
# `as float` on something that is ALREADY a float. This is that cast alone.
# Expected: 3.000000
void main():
    float x = 3.0
    float y = x as float
    print(f"{y}")
